      "Language": "dut",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 38-year-old woman was admitted to the emergency department with vomiting, diarrhoea and abdominal pain since four days. She used anticoagulant drugs because of venous thromboembolism. Echography of the abdomen revealed a subcapsular hematoma of the liver. The patient recovered after bloodtransfusion and conservative treatment."},
